{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471855-sorcery-blood-magic-and-infernalism","id":1471855,"title":"Sorcery, Blood Magic and Infernalism","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-05T13:35:10-08:00","id":1471855,"title":"Sorcery, Blood Magic and Infernalism","content":"In the supplement for Mage &quot;The Sorcerer&quot; there is some room for conversion from sorcerer to vampire.at page 55, including an example: a sorceress called Chula versed in Shapeshifting, Conjuring and Ephemera that - after the Embrace - developes Protean, Thaumaturgy and Necromancy ( despite being a Toreador ).<br /> <br /> Then, there are some hints at possible crossover between Sorcery and vampiric Disciplines: a flaw - Blood Magic - that force the sorcerer to burn or bleed his own blood in addition to Willpower to fuel his magic ( Sorcerer Revised, page 56 ) and also hints that the sorcerer could have learned magic from a vampiric mentor or from stolen vampiric tomes.<br /> <br /> There's a 5 point merit that allows to play a Ghoul sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Finally, there's a sidebar about sorcerers and infernalism at page 83, including the option to buy dots in various Paths through Infernal Pacts.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> In the Dark Ages: Tome of Secrets, some room is left for ghouls learning the Path of Blood ( Thaumaturgy )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Path Magic Path-based magic has appeared in many different World of Darkness books, including Hunters Hunted II. Greater witches may learn the \u201cHedge Magic\u201d Paths there, along with any appropriate Psychic Numina. Adapting Blood Magic If you prefer, you may also adapt magical Disciplines such as Necromancy, Thaumaturgy, or Koldunic Sorcery into mortal equivalents. Witches might learn rituals as well. Paths and rituals with powers that affect vampires but not a wide spectrum of other beings are generally unavailable. For example, mortal witches cannot usually learn an equiv\u0002alent of the Tremere\u2019s Potestas Vitae (also called the Path of Blood). You may make an exception for ghouls </div> </div> </div>Let's take a look at the Path of Blood, more specifically the level 3 and 4 powers:<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Blood of Potency<br /> The thaumaturge gains such control over his own blood that he may effectively \u201cconcentrate\u201d it, making it more powerful for a short time. In effect, he may temporarily lower his own Generation with this power. This power may be used only once per night.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Theft of Vitae<br /> A thaumaturge using this power siphons vitae from her subject. She need never come in contact with the subject \u2014 blood literally streams out in a physical torrent from the subject to the Kindred (though it is often mystically absorbed and need not enter through the mouth).<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> So, here's the questions:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>1- Could a sorcerer-ghoul combine his sorcery ( Willpower and living soul ) with the power of Vitae to develope Disciplines of higher level?<br /> [ example: a sorcerer specialized in Alchemy - 5 dots - with 13th generation vitae in his body and some stolen tomes of Thaumaturgy tries to raise his Path of Blood over 1 dot, probably by &quot;refining&quot; the vitae into alchemical elixirs ]</i></b><br /> <br /> <i><b>2- Could the above sorcerer-ghoul strike an Infernal Pact to raise his pseudo-Discipline as he would with Dark Thaumaturgy?<br /> <br /> 3- Could the above freak use Blood of Potency to raise the generation of his stolen vitae?<br /> <br /> 4- Could he drain vitae from common mortals by using Theft of Vitae? </b></i><br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Last little thing:<br /> <br /> if a vampire can turn into a mortal through a costly ( 9 points ) Investment, or get some aspect of his curse lifted by a little less costly Merit ( Blasphemous Pacts, 6 free points )..could a mortal go the oppsite direction and gain some aspect of the vampiric curse / power through a Merit ( Blasphemous Pact ) or Investment?<br /> For example, having a &quot;virtual generation&quot;, being able to convert mortal blood into Vitae... mabye also being able to perform Diablerie?<br /> <br /> - beside, I've found a level 5 Dark Thaumaturgy ritual that allows to &quot;drink&quot; the soul of a common mortal:<br /> <br /> <i>Soul Leech: The Infernalist with this power can draw souls out of the recently deceased with a successful Wits + Intimidation roll (difficulty of the soul's Willpower). The Infernalist cannot retain the souls, and drawing them out with this ritual destroys them while replenishing the Infernalist. Each soul thus absorbed gives the Infernalist five Blood Points and heals one wound. The Infernalist also receives a rush, stronger than any blood drinking could give. Souls go through complete agony during these few moments. They appear as vaporish clouds of swirling light wisping around the Infernalist, making terrible moaning sounds for the entire duration. The faces of the dead can be seen in the vapor. </i> <br /> <br /> The next question is could a Ghoul use that Rite to consume the soul of a fellow mortal?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 01-05-2022, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T14:49:56-08:00","id":1471861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471855-sorcery-blood-magic-and-infernalism#post1471855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<b><i>1- Could a sorcerer-ghoul combine his sorcery ( Willpower and living soul ) with the power of Vitae to develope Disciplines of higher level?<br /> [ example: a sorcerer specialized in Alchemy - 5 dots - with 13th generation vitae in his body and some stolen tomes of Thaumaturgy tries to raise his Path of Blood over 1 dot, probably by &quot;refining&quot; the vitae into alchemical elixirs ]</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? It's really ST fiat at that point. There aren't any rules for how the system interacts.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers in Sorcerer Revised could copy disciplines up to 3 dots, but doing so isn't normally permanent. Frequently using those potions would be a good enough excuse to buy discipline dots up to 3, but at Ghoul XP costs(15xdot) it'd be a waste of XP.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471855-sorcery-blood-magic-and-infernalism#post1471855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>2- Could the above sorcerer-ghoul strike an Infernal Pact to raise his pseudo-Discipline as he would with Dark Thaumaturgy?</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You can technically get any power for the right infernal pact, even gifts or wan kuei disciplines. You wouldn't even need to raise things with sorcerery and XP first.<br /> <br /> The issue comes from the fact that the price isn't xp....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471855-sorcery-blood-magic-and-infernalism#post1471855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>3- Could the above freak use Blood of Potency to raise the generation of his stolen vitae?</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? Technically you can your generation on stolen vitae, but you wouldn't be raising your stolen vitae's generation, you'd be raining Your generation. Which gets weird considering your character is a ghoul.<br /> <br /> You'd have to figure a base generation to use for ghouls, which is an issue that's come up before. Others on the board settled on using 16 as the starting gen to raise from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471855-sorcery-blood-magic-and-infernalism#post1471855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>4- Could he drain vitae from common mortals by using Theft of Vitae? </i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to re-check the rules, but depending on edition, theft of vitae had rules for feeding from mortals usingit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471855-sorcery-blood-magic-and-infernalism#post1471855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- - -<br /> <br /> Last little thing:<br /> <br /> if a vampire can turn into a mortal through a costly ( 9 points ) Investment, or get some aspect of his curse lifted by a little less costly Merit ( Blasphemous Pacts, 6 free points )..could a mortal go the oppsite direction and gain some aspect of the vampiric curse / power through a Merit ( Blasphemous Pact ) or Investment?<br /> For example, having a &quot;virtual generation&quot;, being able to convert mortal blood into Vitae... mabye also being able to perform Diablerie?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not? I'm pretty sure the demon will try to just do the easy thing and turn you into a high-gen vampire though. It is a demon after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471855-sorcery-blood-magic-and-infernalism#post1471855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- beside, I've found a level 5 Dark Thaumaturgy ritual that allows to &quot;drink&quot; the soul of a common mortal:<br /> <br /> <i>Soul Leech: The Infernalist with this power can draw souls out of the recently deceased with a successful Wits + Intimidation roll (difficulty of the soul's Willpower). The Infernalist cannot retain the souls, and drawing them out with this ritual destroys them while replenishing the Infernalist. Each soul thus absorbed gives the Infernalist five Blood Points and heals one wound. The Infernalist also receives a rush, stronger than any blood drinking could give. Souls go through complete agony during these few moments. They appear as vaporish clouds of swirling light wisping around the Infernalist, making terrible moaning sounds for the entire duration. The faces of the dead can be seen in the vapor. </i><br /> <br /> The next question is could a Ghoul use that Rite to consume the soul of a fellow mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can perform it? Yes. The effects of the ritual are clearly spelled out in the ritual's description. Whoever's casting it shouldn't matter.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't give you diablerie benefits, just blood and wound healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T00:57:32-08:00","id":1471913,"title":"","content":"There are 16th generation vampires now (as of BJD), so I'd make ghouls 17th generation. And if a 17th generation comes along, I'd bump them down to 18th, and so on, so that ghouls are always one step lower than the highest generation vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T03:31:46-08:00","id":1471919,"title":"","content":"I simply disagree with the very notion of ascribing a Generation to Ghouls in that way.<br /> <br /> While humans they simply don't have Generation as an aspect of their being. And while you don't affect the Vitae in your system, the level of Discipline permitted by the Generation of your Regnant <b>is</b> how the very concept of Generation manifests in a Ghoul.<br /> <br /> So much so that it doesn't actually depends on that Vitae still being present in your system at the moment, just if it is what empowered you as a Ghoul in the first place. You get a kick from a 7th Gen Regnant, even if you spend the Vitae right away you're still the Ghoul of a 7th Gen Regnant at least 'till the end of a month, arguably for some months even if you refresh on weaker Vitae later.<br /> <br /> Then I'd say simply lower the effective Regnant's Gen and be done with it. And any effect that look for actual Generation still finds the same thing it found in the first place when looking at a Ghoul: this is not a Vampire. If you want to be treated as one... well, you <b>do</b> have Thaumaturgy, figure out some ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}